function info(k){const T={about:`<h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">About &amp; accuracy</h2><p><b>What this is.</b> A prototype of a Western NY storm-safety app: local risk, a readiness plan, and a trusted circle of family, neighbors and verified helpers.</p><p><b>What is simulated.</b> Weather, radar, outages, shelters and users are a replay of a blizzard, not live data. The live NWS card shows real data when the app can reach it.</p><p><b>How risk is scored.</b> Snowfall rate counts most, then wind, then neighborhood vulnerability, on a 0–100 scale.</p><p><b>Accuracy.</b> Not measured yet. Backtests against the 2014 and 2022 storms need the real model, and results will be published here.</p>`,terms:`<h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Terms in plain language</h2><p>Cold Path is not a substitute for 911. In an emergency, call 911 first.</p><p>Helpers are community members. Verified means we checked a government ID. Never pay a helper or share passwords or bank details. Report anyone who asks.</p><p>We share your status and location only with the people you choose, and you can delete your data any time.</p>`,api:`<h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Open API &amp; other cities</h2><p class="sm mut">This is the planned spec. These endpoints are not live yet.</p><pre>GET /risk?lat=42.89&amp;lon=-78.88&amp;horizon=6\n→ {"risk":72,"range":[64,80],"snow_in_hr":2.4,"updated":"…"}\n\nGET /route?from=42.9,-78.84&amp;to=42.85,-78.75&amp;mode=safest\n→ {"km":9.8,"eta_min":24,"worst_risk":61,"path":[…]}\n\nGET /storm-alerts?lat=…&amp;lon=…</pre><p><b>Bring Cold Path to your city</b></p><ol><li>Swap in your shoreline, county lines and road graph.</li><li>Point the data adapters at your NWS office and local data.</li><li>Load verified shelters and warming centers.</li><li>Add your languages with native translators.</li><li>Partner with your emergency office and 211.</li></ol>`};modal(T[k])}
